# Compute side of the `pioneer` target (the APS cluster's GPU queue): the standalone runner and LaueMatching with the
# GPU stream daemon. No database, Redis, web server, Globus or MPI (a job is one process on one GPU).
# `make lock` compiles compute-gpu.lock with dev's versions, like compute.lock; the dev env does not install it.
#
# Python 3.12 in a conda-forge env from environment-gpu.yml (environment.yml with conda-forge's CUDA compiler): numpy,
# h5py and cffi come from conda-forge and are left out of the lock. lauelab is not in the lock either: install it
# from GitHub with --no-deps at the commit pinned in scripts/setup.sh.
#
# laue-index ships only an sdist: build it with its CUDA binaries required (LAUEMATCHING_CUDA=require) and the env's
# nvcc on PATH, so an install without LaueMatchingGPUStream fails instead of leaving the CPU binaries alone
# (docs/runbooks/remote-execution.md, "The APS GPU target").

PyYAML==6.0.3
psutil==7.2.2

# lauelab's own runtime dependencies (it is installed with --no-deps), as in compute.in.
